  "id": "COMPOUND:29645 - PROTEIN:5856",
  "verbalization": "Caryptoside is linked to SNU-387 through a series of molecular targets, all of which are classified as MIPs. These MIPs are identified as targets of various compounds, including (3R)-5,8,9-trimethoxy-2,2-dimethyl-3,4-dihydropyrano[2,3-b]quinolin-3-ol, 5-hydroxy-6,8-dimethoxy-2,3-dimethylbenzo[G]chromen-4-one, and a complex ester compound. The shared target of all three compounds is SNU-387, suggesting a potential mechanism of action involving these MIPs. The evidence supports a relationship where Caryptoside may act through these MIPs to influence SNU-387, possibly by modulating its activity or interaction. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible role for Caryptoside in targeting a common molecular interface, which could be a key mechanism in its biological effects.",
